{"words": [{"text": "فِيهِ", "translation": "In it"}, {"text": "ءَايَـٰتٌۢ", "translation": "(are) signs"}, {"text": "بَيِّنَـٰتٌۭ", "translation": "clear"}, {"text": "مَّقَامُ", "translation": "standing place"}, {"text": "إِبْرَٰهِيمَ ۖ", "translation": "(of) Ibrahim"}, {"text": "وَمَن", "translation": "and whoever"}, {"text": "دَخَلَهُۥ", "translation": "enters it "}, {"text": "كَانَ", "translation": "is"}, {"text": "ءَامِنًۭا ۗ", "translation": "safe"}, {"text": "وَلِلَّهِ", "translation": "And (due) to Allah"}, {"text": "عَلَى", "translation": "upon"}, {"text": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translation": "the mankind"}, {"text": "حِجُّ", "translation": "(is) pilgrimage"}, {"text": "ٱلْبَيْتِ", "translation": "(of) the House"}, {"text": "مَنِ", "translation": "(for one) who"}, {"text": "ٱسْتَطَاعَ", "translation": "is able"}, {"text": "إِلَيْهِ", "translation": "to [it]"}, {"text": "سَبِيلًۭا ۚ", "translation": "(find) a way"}, {"text": "وَمَن", "translation": "And whoever"}, {"text": "كَفَرَ", "translation": "disbelieved"}, {"text": "فَإِنَّ", "translation": "then indeed"}, {"text": "ٱللَّهَ", "translation": "Allah"}, {"text": "غَنِىٌّ", "translation": "(is) free from need"}, {"text": "عَنِ", "translation": "of"}, {"text": "ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ", "translation": "the universe"}], "sahih": "In it are clear signs [such as] the standing place of Abraham. And whoever enters it [i.e., the Ḥaram] shall be safe. And [due] to Allāh from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way. But whoever disbelieves [i.e., refuses] - then indeed, Allāh is free from need of the worlds.1"}